;; og:preserve-this V7 (#41): drawable-tree-region-prim has no vis geometry to unpack.
;; Without this override the call falls through to drawable-tree's generic per-node
;; byte-offset writer, which derives its write offset from the tree's own first node
;; id; region-prim data is not a fragment-id tree, so that offset is wrong for this
;; type. Found alongside the drawable-group gap while tracing #41's all-zero vis-bits.
;; Matches jak3's landed body verbatim (goal_src/jak3/engine/level/region.gc:45).
(defmethod unpack-vis ((this drawable-tree-region-prim) (arg0 (pointer int8)) (arg1 (pointer int8)))
  arg1
  )

;; og:preserve-this issue 595 / trigvol dossier: the rest of region.gc lands here,
;; transplanted from jak3's landed goal_src/jak3/engine/level/region.gc:11-667 and
;; adjudicated line for line against this worktree's own clean decode
;; (region_disasm.gc). region-execute above stays the retail-faithful empty stub;
;; jakx's real per-frame driver lives in jakx-region-driver (region-driver.gc), not
;; here, because retail moved the positional input into net-player for split-screen.
;; Two numeric divergences from jak3's text, both proven from this worktree's own
;; decode rather than assumed: mem-usage's memory-usage-block bucket indices are
;; 49/50 here where jak3 uses 50/51 (jakx's usage-block table has one fewer entry
